      "writtenOn": "2026-07-16T12:31:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Skipping reclamation avoids returning kernel-owned buffers prematurely, but deletion then discards the partial-chain, RX-ring, and fill-ring buffer references, as well as the libxdp program handle. Repeated detach failures can therefore exhaust the VPP buffer pool. Could we retain the device on failure, or quiesce through socket teardown while preserving enough ownership state to reclaim the buffers afterward?",
      "parentUuid": "89def6b5_1559cfd2",
      "revId": "a9dfe92cfabc0e97a5a1f6dc0203d4c8e7f0e2b4",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
