      "writtenOn": "2026-07-16T12:31:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The 18-segment check covers copy mode, but zero-copy validates against the device-specific `xdp_zc_max_segs`, which can be lower. A chain exceeding that limit is consumed as invalid without completion entries, so VPP never frees its buffers. Could we also handle the zero-copy limit, or reject multi-buffer zero-copy when it cannot be enforced safely?",
      "parentUuid": "ce7a1e81_c18408ae",
      "revId": "a9dfe92cfabc0e97a5a1f6dc0203d4c8e7f0e2b4",
